{"step_index":2449,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:03:31Z","content":"### 🏗️ Blueprint for a Best-in-Class Storage Architecture for SnapDialer\n\nTo elevate SnapDialer’s storage layer from a functional snapshot engine to an enterprise-grade, best-in-class PWA database capable of effortlessly managing **50,000+ educator leads, high-resolution field card photos, and call logs with sub-millisecond query response times**, here are the specific architectural recommendations:\n\n---\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                         BEST-IN-CLASS STORAGE TOPOLOGY                                  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Granular Multi-Table Storage (Dexie.js)   ➔ Normalized leads, lists, call logs        │\n│ 2. Isolated Binary Blob Store                ➔ High-res card photos separated from JSON  │\n│ 3. Compound B-Tree Indexing Engine           ➔ [school + disposition + priority] indexes  │\n│ 4. Relaxed-Durability Ingestion Pipeline     ➔ 10x faster bulk CSV / OCR card batching   │\n│ 5. Dedicated WebWorker Offloading            ➔ UI thread locked at 60-120 FPS            │\n│ 6. Storage Quota & Persistence Observability ➔ Real-time MB/GB usage diagnostics         │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Recommendation 1: Decouple Big Binary Blobs (Card Photos) from Metadata\n\n#### The Problem:\nC\n<truncated 3442 bytes>\ndicated `StorageWorker.ts`:\n- **Image Compression:** Canvas resize and JPEG compression run inside an `OffscreenCanvas` in the worker thread.\n- **CSV & Excel Parsing:** Parses raw CSV text and normalizes column headers off the main thread.\n- **Full-Text Search:** Indexes educator notes and card inquiries without interfering with dialer HUD gestures.\n\n---\n\n### Recommendation 5: Storage Observability & Quota Dashboard\n\n#### The Problem:\nSales representatives need confidence that their field data is securely stored and that the browser will never silently evict their pipeline.\n\n#### The Solution:\nExpose native browser storage diagnostics in the **Settings Screen** ([`SettingsScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx)):\n- **Persistence State:** `navigator.storage.persisted()` ➔ Display green badge: `🛡️ Storage Locked & Protected from Eviction`.\n- **Disk Usage Meter:** `navigator.storage.estimate()` ➔ Display real-time capacity (e.g., `💾 18.4 MB used of 42.8 GB available`).\n- **Automated Health Check:** If unpersisted, prompts the user to add the app to their Home Screen to lock permanent PWA storage rights.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Summary Comparison: Current vs. Proposed Best-in-Class\n\n| Metric / Feature | Current Implementation | Proposed Best-in-Class |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Storage Architecture** | Monolithic JSON snapshot (`'root_state'`) | Granular Multi-Table Dexie.js Object Stores |\n| **Card Photos Handling** | Stored inside Lead JSON (High memory footprint) | Isolated `lead_photos` Binary Blob Store (Zero memory drag) |\n| **Query Complexity** | In-Memory JavaScript Array Filter ($O(N)$) | B-Tree Compound Indexes ($O(\\log N)$) |\n| **Bulk Write Speed** | Re-serializes full state snapshot | `{ durability: 'relaxed' }` Chunked `bulkPut` (10x faster) |\n| **UI Responsiveness** | Main thread parsing | Background WebWorker with `OffscreenCanvas` |\n| **Storage Visibility** | Basic contact counters | Live Disk Meter (`MB / GB`) & Persistence Guard |","thinking":"**Prioritizing Best Practices**\n\nI'm now focusing on specific recommendations to elevate the dialer's storage solution to best-in-class status, *without* code changes this turn. I'm prioritizing actionable insights based on the user's prior assessment request. I aim to identify key areas for improvement in design, performance, and maintainability. My focus is on providing concrete, non-code-related recommendations to enhance the storage.\n\n\n**Refining Indexing Strategies**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on optimizing Dexie.js indexes to accelerate dialing and geofiltering functionality, and thus performance. I am devising multi-column indexes, such as `leads: 'id, list_id, school, priority_tier, last_disposition, [list_id+priority_tier+last_disposition]'`, as well as a separate `settings` table with a key-value structure. The goal is to maximize data retrieval efficiency without changing the code this turn.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
