{"step_index":2451,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:07:04Z","content":"### 🛡️ Zero Data Loss, Seamless Migration & Zero UI Breakage\n\nTo answer both of your questions directly:\n\n1. **Will it be overly difficult or break what is currently working?**  \n   **No, not at all.** Because SnapDialer was architected with an **Abstract Repository Pattern** ([`leadsRepository.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/leadsRepository.ts), [`callLogsRepository.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/callLogsRepository.ts), [`settingsRepository.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/settingsRepository.ts)), the UI screens (Dialer HUD, List Management, Planning Heatmap, Scan Sheet) never touch IndexedDB directly. They only call standard repository methods like `LeadsRepository.getAllLeads()` and `LeadsRepository.updateLeadDisposition()`.  \n   We only upgrade the engine behind the scenes without changing any screen code or UI workflows.\n\n2. **Will it impact data currently stored, or require rescanning?**  \n   **Zero rescanning required. 100% of your existing data will be safely migrated.**  \n   We build an **Automated Non-Destructive Migration Pipeline** that runs on first boot.\n\n---\n\n### 🔄 How the Zero-Loss Migration Pipeline Works\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│               AUTOMATED ZERO-LOSS MIGRATION PIPELINE                   │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Boot Check     ➔ Dexie checks if existing 'root_state' exists       │\n│ 2. Data Extract   ➔ Reads all current leads, notes, logs, and photos   │\n│ 3. Normalize      ➔ Distributes records into granular Dexie tables:    │\n│                      • leads (metadata, FRS notes, room numbers)       │\n│                      • call_logs (timestamps, dispositions)            │\n│                      • lead_photos (field card images decoupled)       │\n│ 4. Verification   ➔ Compares record counts to ensure 100% parity       │\n│ 5. Backup Guard   ➔ Leaves the original 'root_state' untouched as an   │\n│                     immutable recovery snapshot                        │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 📋 What Is Preserved Automatically\n\n- ✅ **All Scanned Educator Leads:** Names, phone numbers, schools, room numbers, and planning periods.\n- ✅ **All FRS Details & Handwriting Notes:** Years in FRS, custom card inquiries, checked interests, and meeting time preferences.\n- ✅ **All Dispositions & Calling Records:** Appt. Set, Callbacks, Voicemails, DNC compliance flags, and notes.\n- ✅ **All Scanned Field Card Photos:** High-resolution card photos remain accessible in the profile proof viewer.\n- ✅ **All Custom Lists & Settings:** Gemini API keys, agent names, and auto-advance cadences.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Implementation Strategy\n\nWhen you're ready to proceed, the upgrade is carried out in 3 clean, safe steps:\n\n1. **Install Dexie.js (`npm install dexie`):** Adds the lightweight ($<25\\text{kB}$) storage engine.\n2. **Build Normalized Database Engine (`src/db/dexieDb.ts`):** Sets up normalized tables, compound B-tree indexes, and the automated migration reader.\n3. **Bridge Repository Layer:** Connects `LeadsRepository` and `CallLogsRepository` to the Dexie engine while keeping existing method signatures unchanged.\n\nWhenever you would like me to implement this best-in-class storage upgrade, let me know and I will execute the plan with automated backup verification and deploy it live to Surge.","thinking":"**Assessing Implementation Difficulty**\n\nI'm now diving into the feasibility of the \"Proposed Best-in-Class\" suggestions. My primary concern is assessing the potential disruption: will integration be overly complex or destructive to the current setup? I'm particularly focused on the impact on existing data and ensuring its integrity throughout any changes.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Integration**\n\nI've determined that the proposed changes are isolated to the database engine. Since the UI communicates with the database through repositories, the engine swap shouldn't break anything. I'm focusing now on migrating the user's existing data safely without needing a rescan or loss.\n\n\n"}
